  "features": [
    "Per-loop thread-local monotonic state measures only actual kernel wait boundaries; callbacks remain active time and metric state is released with loop teardown.",
    "Native performance factory occupies the checked boundary after the contiguous pinned dispatcher without changing existing IDs or class layouts.",
    "Event-loop utilization returns measured cumulative POSIX idle/active times and supports one-snapshot and two-snapshot differences; main and worker controls pass."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Windows libuv utilization is explicitly unimplemented; the native reader reports this rather than returning fabricated zero telemetry. Linux execution remains unverified.",
    "Startup milestones, full resource/observer behavior, wider performance semantics and lifetime accounting beyond ordinary worker/loop shutdown remain open under #869.",
    "Initial misplaced instrumentation and namespace compile failures are retained without passing credit. The final executable differed from the earlier build and all selected scopes were rerun on it.",
    "The prior ICU contradiction #872, full Bun suite, remaining native/API ownership and Release/ASAN/all-platform verification remain open under #66.",
    "Pickier reports no errors and one quote-style warning in the existing mixed-style performance module."
  ],
